WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:02.240
[Jake:] Most people say, that living in Los Angeles

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:05.500
Requires you to own a car in order to survive

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:07.580
Today, I challenge that assumption

00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:09.860
With the rise in electric motor and battery tech

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:12.440
utilizing alternative electric transpo

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:16.840
Like electric bicycles, is more viable than it has ever been before

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:20.660
But have we gotten to the point of being able to ditch our cars altogether?

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:22.520
Let's find out

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:24.540
For the next week, I will remove all...

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:26.600
automotive transportation from my life

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:29.140
and replace it with only an electric bike

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:31.520
[Electric bike whirring]

00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:39.880
[Background music]

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:49.900
[Sam:] Gangster style

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:54.140
[Jake:] I only live about eight miles from the studio, which means that using an electric bicycle for that

00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:55.600
is totally possible

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:58.580
Also, I gotta make up for some of the gas guzzling this truck does

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:01.800
[Knocking on the door]

00:01:02.060 --> 00:01:02.800
[Background chatter]

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:03.620
[Jake:] Good to see ya

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:04.480
[Nick:] Hey Steven. Nick

00:01:04.480 --> 00:01:05.480
Good to meet ya man

00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:07.580
[Store person:] The most common thing people, you know, you're gonna think about

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:09.240
what you're saving on is gas, right?

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:12.760
but you've got like, a wear and tear on the vehicles. You're not doing as many oil changes...

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:14.060
tire changes - all that stuff

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:15.580
The miles are so low now

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:19.120
that his insurance is almost cut in half, 'coz he's under seventy five, hundred miles a year

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:20.780
so its considered a luxury vehicle

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:24.040
Of course you get the exercise, he said the biggest thing he got though from commuting

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:25.600
was his zen time

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:28.280
[Niko:] Changing the Sam and Niko name is a big deal

00:01:28.280 --> 00:01:30.400
Sam and I have called it the Sam and Niko channel

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:31.940
ever since it was just me and him

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:34.240
We're changing the name from "Sam and Niko" to "Corridor Crew"

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:37.380
But we can't half-ass it. We need to do it right. It's not just a name change

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:39.200
It's a full-on branding change

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:40.880
If somebody hasn't come to the channel in a little while

00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:42.200
and they see that it says Corridor Crew

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:44.660
they need to know that it's the same channel and it's the same people

00:01:44.660 --> 00:01:46.400
we need to enhance it for art

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:48.600
Both Sam and I have been pretty strict, saying

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:50.960
we need to have everything set to go at the same time

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:52.940
the little intro to the video, the channel name change

00:01:52.940 --> 00:01:54.280
the icon change and

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:55.600
most importantly the banner

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:58.520
The banner needs to be good. It needs to be photos of the crew

00:01:58.520 --> 00:02:00.680
It needs to speak to the team that we are

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:04.900
So Sam has told me he's going to dedicate his passion and his artistry

00:02:04.900 --> 00:02:07.660
to getting a really solid banner photograph for us

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:10.320
Sounds like he was a pretty cool vision for it and I'm looking forward to it

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:11.000
So...

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:12.800
I'll wait for him to call me in for a picture

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:15.800
[Sam:] Oh God, why is this picture day so stressful?

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:16.980
I'm taking pictures...

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:19.580
but I don't really have a direction. So I'm just gonna wing it

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:20.800
See that pink line?

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:21.760
[Off camera Nick:] Yes

00:02:22.460 --> 00:02:23.200
[Sam:] Feet on that, yeah

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:24.420
Generally toes at

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:25.380
Look like a cool guy

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:26.600
Take a baby step backwards

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:28.940
Baby step forward again. Like, what will I shoot next?

00:02:29.060 --> 00:02:30.100
[Camera clicks]

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:34.060
[Wren:] That's such a great photo. That's-- that's profile photo worthy

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:35.300
[Off screen Nick:] Hey Gabe

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:36.920
[Camera clicks]

00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:37.960
[Sam:] Pretty natural

00:02:37.960 --> 00:02:39.720
Just take a baby step toward me. Yeah there we go

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:41.500
Straight on. Go straight again

00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:43.400
Uh, relax your arms just a little bit

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:45.800
...about what to write next

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:47.620
Lighting setup...

00:02:47.620 --> 00:02:49.860
I chose the first light

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:53.480
that was plugged in. It's an LED blanket. We played around with those last year

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:56.880
You get this nice soft diffusion. Here, you'll realize they're gangster style

00:02:57.380 --> 00:02:58.460
Yeah...

00:02:58.880 --> 00:03:03.560
[Off screen Jake:] The bike I'll be using is the Blix Comfort Prima from the Blix electric bike company

00:03:03.580 --> 00:03:06.660
It comes equipped with the Shimano Steps, mid drive electric motor

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:10.280
Which is an assisted power system that lets you bike as you pedal

00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:12.400
There is no throttle and no special knowledge required

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:15.180
All you do is get on the bike and the steps motor

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:16.080
assists you along

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:18.880
The aluminum alloy frame is built specifically for this motor

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:22.700
and when combined with the 700 centimeter, double-wall alloy wheels

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:25.240
and padded leather saddle and leather grips

00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:27.040
it delivers a comfortable smooth ride

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:28.480
It's a commuter bike...

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:30.480
and commuting is exactly what I'll be doing

00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:32.120
It's 13 miles

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:34.160
[Sam:] 13 miles? Okay, 13 miles

00:03:34.160 --> 00:03:37.240
So you're gonna be getting here- It's gonna take you like, yeah, 35, 40 minutes

00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:38.980
I mean that's a lot of minutes

00:03:38.980 --> 00:03:42.580
I mean, I would be interested to see them as possible, because from my experience in LA

00:03:42.580 --> 00:03:45.900
is like, there's not even sidewalks. And everyone here drives like a maniac

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:48.440
So it's like, literally the whole world is fighting against you

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:49.480
[Jake:] Yeah, kinda

00:03:49.480 --> 00:03:52.980
I am now officially on my first electric bike commute

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:54.820
I'm gonna be mostly taking two rivers

00:03:54.820 --> 00:03:58.020
Meaning I'm gonna go about, an extra mile

00:03:58.020 --> 00:03:59.720
in a direction that I don't want to go

00:03:59.980 --> 00:04:02.940
However, there is a shortcut if...

00:04:02.940 --> 00:04:05.460
I take a set of abandoned train tracks

00:04:05.460 --> 00:04:07.780
I'll save about a mile on my trip

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:10.400
Do not take the train tracks

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:12.280
These are active train tracks, all right?

00:04:12.280 --> 00:04:16.040
and currently I'm stuck, somewhere over the 710 freeway

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:20.560
Alright. This is the river path

00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:25.860
The thing I really like about this assisted power system, is that you can still get a workout in

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:29.660
Given the time it takes to work out at home, drive to the studio

00:04:29.660 --> 00:04:34.340
and the time it takes to drive back at night, I actually think I saved myself a half hour a day

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:38.180
[Sam:] LA is one of the most sprawled out cities in the entire United States

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:42.120
Honestly, like, I love biking. I've loved biking my whole life and it's great

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:45.200
And then once I moved to LA, I stopped. The city was just fighting me

00:04:45.220 --> 00:04:47.400
It's kind of scary to bike 'coz cars are like...

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:49.080
[Jake:] Could this go horribly wrong?

00:04:49.420 --> 00:04:52.240
Yes, and if it does then we all know

00:04:52.240 --> 00:04:56.220
that LA is the most non pedestrian friendly city on the history of

00:04:56.680 --> 00:04:59.040
On this history of the planet. Which it probably is

00:04:59.160 --> 00:05:01.160
[Multiple car horns]

00:05:01.160 --> 00:05:03.160
[Car horn]

00:05:04.020 --> 00:05:06.740
[Multiple car horns]

00:05:07.880 --> 00:05:09.880
[Car horn]

00:05:10.600 --> 00:05:12.260
[Bike brakes squeaking]

00:05:12.260 --> 00:05:14.260
[Jake:] It's so fucking sketch around here

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:17.820
This is clearly an area that's not set up

00:05:17.820 --> 00:05:20.780
for bicycle transportation, whatsoever

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:22.900
Definitely 45 minutes

00:05:22.900 --> 00:05:24.340
Hey, look, there's Wren

00:05:24.460 --> 00:05:26.420
[Wren:] Oh hey. Dude you made it! Nice!

00:05:26.420 --> 00:05:27.420
[Off screen Jake:] I made it dude

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:28.900
Day three

00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:30.190
commute home

00:05:30.190 --> 00:05:32.720
And there's two things I've noticed so far

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:34.320
Number one - Zen

00:05:34.320 --> 00:05:36.840
You get a lot of time for...

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:39.020
thought and reflection

00:05:39.180 --> 00:05:40.840
when you are

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:44.380
out here effectively alone after a day's work

00:05:44.380 --> 00:05:46.200
you get a lot of time to think about it

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:51.580
and on your way in you get a lot of time to think about your way in and what you're gonna do that day

00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:54.400
So that's really really nice. I really really like that

00:05:54.400 --> 00:05:56.580
Number two however - Know your gear

00:05:56.600 --> 00:06:00.600
know what you might need, uh, along the way

00:06:00.600 --> 00:06:05.940
and the only way you really get to know your gear is by using the gear that you have

00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:12.240
I've already had to cancel an appointment

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:15.740
I've been trying to go to the eye doctor for about a month now

00:06:15.740 --> 00:06:18.600
and today I finally had an opportunity to go

00:06:19.080 --> 00:06:24.360
but there's no possible way that I could take my bike to the eye doctor and

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:29.500
Get over to downtown LA for another meeting that we have in time

00:06:29.500 --> 00:06:33.000
If I had a car, probably would have been able to make both of those things.

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:34.960
but it's just too far and not enough time

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:39.640
This isn't a fun day because I'm carrying a lot of weight in this backpack right here

00:06:39.640 --> 00:06:44.140
I'm carrying airsoft rifles. They're heavy. They have batteries. They have magazines with bb's in them

00:06:44.140 --> 00:06:46.300
I gotta take these all the way to work, I don't have a car

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:48.040
There's only one way to do that. Grind it out

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:51.720
Between the filming and the traffic today, it's taking me

00:06:51.720 --> 00:06:54.380
It's gonna take me over an hour. Look at this.

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:56.920
So every time I have to cross the road

00:06:56.920 --> 00:07:03.140
I need to wait a super long time for traffic because you have to roll with traffic across intersections

00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:07.900
This is--

00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:10.760
To do this everyday and to replace it with your car

00:07:11.380 --> 00:07:12.220
is

00:07:12.220 --> 00:07:13.300
not

00:07:13.300 --> 00:07:14.320
Not enjoyable

00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:18.200
[Christian:] Uh... So I know we've been planning to change the branding and I know the name

00:07:18.520 --> 00:07:19.900
for the new Corridor Crew

00:07:20.500 --> 00:07:22.720
But honestly Sam's been tucked away in the cave

00:07:22.920 --> 00:07:26.160
during this whole process. So I have no idea what the new assets look like at all

00:07:26.360 --> 00:07:28.000
[Wren:] Is it official is it flipped?

00:07:28.180 --> 00:07:29.660
[Niko:] We're changing the channel name right now

00:07:29.660 --> 00:07:30.380
How you doing it Jake

00:07:30.380 --> 00:07:32.540
[Jake:] like, I'm doing it right now

00:07:32.540 --> 00:07:34.680
[Wren:] Question are we gonna have Crew shirts now?

00:07:35.020 --> 00:07:35.920
[Collective comments]

00:07:35.920 --> 00:07:36.680
[Jake:] Heck yeah

00:07:36.680 --> 00:07:38.540
[Wren:] Once we get the fancy new store--

00:07:38.540 --> 00:07:40.440
[Niko:] Once Jake has the merch store back up

00:07:40.440 --> 00:07:42.300
[Jake:] Just send them the new designs man.

00:07:42.300 --> 00:07:43.060
[Wren:] Black on black.

00:07:43.060 --> 00:07:45.080
[Jake:] You guys just wait trust me

00:07:45.080 --> 00:07:47.640
The wait on the merch store is gonna be worth it

00:07:47.640 --> 00:07:48.800
I promise you

00:07:48.860 --> 00:07:50.540
[Drumming]

00:07:50.540 --> 00:07:52.040
[Wren:] Dude...yeah...

00:07:52.920 --> 00:07:54.160
[Cheering]

00:07:54.160 --> 00:07:54.800
[Niko:] So pro!

00:07:54.800 --> 00:07:58.440
[Jake:] Time to announce our 1 million subscribers street meet barbecue

00:07:58.600 --> 00:08:00.580
[Wren:] Maybe not call it street meet barbecue though

00:08:00.580 --> 00:08:02.680
[Jake:] Street meat barbecue dude. It's a meet-up.

00:08:02.840 --> 00:08:07.620
Barbecue, in a park, in LA when we hit 1 million subs

00:08:07.620 --> 00:08:08.960
[Niko:] So hit that sub button

00:08:08.960 --> 00:08:10.600
That's what Jake forgot to end a sentence with

00:08:10.600 --> 00:08:12.860
[Jake:] We'll announce it. We'll probably announce it...not here

00:08:13.020 --> 00:08:16.320
[Niko:] Hit that subscribe button if you want to get us to this park meet

00:08:16.340 --> 00:08:18.740
[Wren:] Don't that mean that like, our viewers are part of the crew?

00:08:19.080 --> 00:08:19.720
[Jake:] Yes

00:08:19.720 --> 00:08:20.400
[Niko:] Yes

00:08:20.400 --> 00:08:23.560
[Wren:] So hit that subscribe button if you want to be part of the Corridor Crew

00:08:23.560 --> 00:08:24.460
Thank you

00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:27.840
[Jake:] Thanks Wren

00:08:28.180 --> 00:08:29.780
[Background music]

00:08:31.180 --> 00:08:33.940
[Off screen Jake:] Putting over 200 miles in on this electric bike

00:08:33.940 --> 00:08:39.130
I've come to the conclusion, that you can actually live in this city without owning a car

00:08:39.340 --> 00:08:43.840
But that said, you're not going to be able to get away with not using cars at all

00:08:43.840 --> 00:08:47.720
you're still gonna need to rent cars, do things like ride-shares from time to time

00:08:47.720 --> 00:08:49.480
just to get around this city

00:08:49.480 --> 00:08:50.220
Why?

00:08:50.220 --> 00:08:55.400
It's 500 square miles and it's been built pretty much from the ground up for cars. But...

00:08:55.400 --> 00:08:58.720
if you can find the efficiency in your life to get by on an electric bike

00:08:58.720 --> 00:09:01.700
You can actually do it and you're gonna save a ton of money that way too

00:09:01.700 --> 00:09:04.320
For me however, I'm not ready to give up cars just yet

00:09:05.260 --> 00:09:09.400
Huge thanks to the Blix bicycle company for hooking us up with the electric bike

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:11.460
if you guys are interested in trying this on your own

00:09:11.500 --> 00:09:14.660
Go to blixbike.com, and use the offer code

00:09:16.260 --> 00:09:18.440
to get $100 off your first bike

00:09:18.740 --> 00:09:20.060
You're welcome

00:09:21.020 --> 00:09:23.020
[Background music]

